  "result": "Reservations with expiry are in. `npm test` passes: 174 tests, 0 failed, including 9 new ones in `test/reservations.test.js`.\n\n- **Store** (`src/store.js`): I added `reserve`, `getAvailable`, `confirm` and `release`, and `removeItem` now checks against available stock. Expiry uses only the store's `clock`.\n- **API** (`src/api.js`): `GET /stock/:sku` now also returns `available`. I added `POST /reservations`, `POST /reservations/:id/confirm` and `DELETE /reservations/:id` with the status codes you listed.\n\nA few behaviours you didn't specify:\n- **`ttlMs`:** it isn't validated. A missing or non-numeric value makes the expiry `NaN`, so that reservation never counts against availability.\n- **`confirm` return value:** `confirm(id)` returns `{ sku, qty }`, because the API needs the SKU for its response.\n- **Expired reservations:** they stay in memory and are never purged. Confirming one keeps returning `RESERVATION_EXPIRED` rather than `RESERVATION_NOT_FOUND`.\n- **Reservation ids:** they look like `res-1`, `res-2` and so on. They are unique within a store but easy to guess.\n- **Other API errors:** `POST /reservations` returns 400 for any error other than `INSUFFICIENT_STOCK`, and the confirm route returns 404 for any error other than `RESERVATION_EXPIRED`.\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
